<title>UK: CIBC releases details of $200 million Yankee FRN.</title>
<headline>CIBC releases details of $200 million Yankee FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>CIBC Wood Gundy said on Tuesday it was sole manager of a $200 million five-year FRN launched in the Yankee market for itself.</p>
<p>The notes, which pay three-month LIBOR flat, mature on May 28, 2002. Payment is due May 28. Denominations are $100,000.</p>
<p>CIBC said the deal had been arranged last Friday. Canada was closed Monday for a holiday.</p>
<p>No other details were made available.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
